{"attachments":[],"author":{"display_name":"Versil","id":"148682928434577408","is_bot":0,"username":"versil"},"author_id":"148682928434577408","channel_id":"863631111585660938","content":"two questions about <#863541645080920105> in The City, and that the pin says you cannot sleep there.\n- are you allowed to moor your ship there at night, if you don't sleep during that time?\n- this one may be a bit of a stretch on the rules so I'll take a straight \"no\" with no explanation. actually nvm, it's Crui's idea so she can word her thoughts better","created_at":"2021-07-13T16:42:38.945000Z","edited_at":null,"id":"864547384360828980","reply_to_id":null,"thread":null,"thread_id":null}
{"attachments":[],"author":{"display_name":"Cruithne","id":"150319814836092928","is_bot":0,"username":"cruithne"},"author_id":"150319814836092928","channel_id":"863631111585660938","content":"so, basically, my thought was that - because V wakes up before curfew but I don't, what happens if someone ALREADY sleeping is taken into the moorage?\n\nso like:\n>Roy wakes up before curfew, Sabrine is still 'asleep' (she doesn't sleep but that's a technicality)\n>Roy pilots the airship to the moorage\n>Sabrine wakes up eventually when the airship is already there","created_at":"2021-07-13T16:43:55.644000Z","edited_at":null,"id":"864547706059096075","reply_to_id":null,"thread":null,"thread_id":null}
{"attachments":[],"author":{"display_name":"Versil","id":"148682928434577408","is_bot":0,"username":"versil"},"author_id":"148682928434577408","channel_id":"863631111585660938","content":"I think the odd thing with the timing here is that we start the long rest roughly the same time, but you OOC don't wake up till later. that's why on one hand it feels like it'd work, but on the other still like a tiny bit of a massive stretch","created_at":"2021-07-13T16:48:31.785000Z","edited_at":null,"id":"864548864278790145","reply_to_id":null,"thread":null,"thread_id":null}
{"attachments":[],"author":{"display_name":"Cruithne","id":"150319814836092928","is_bot":0,"username":"cruithne"},"author_id":"150319814836092928","channel_id":"863631111585660938","content":"honestly, my thought to balance is it is that someone has to be awake in the airship - so Roy wouldn't be able to leave until Sabrine woke up, which would still be a few hours but then he'd be able to go to the pond immediately without curfew shenanigans","created_at":"2021-07-13T16:49:21.303000Z","edited_at":null,"id":"864549071972990998","reply_to_id":null,"thread":null,"thread_id":null}
